      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The increased difficulty in spotting melanoma in darker skin is partly due to melanin masking subtle pigmentary changes, but there are also biological differences in clinical presentation. Studies suggest that melanoma may take on different morphologies and present later in life in darker skin tones. Clinicians should be hyper-vigilant for melanoma in sun-exposed areas that might be overlooked, such as the ears, lips, lower legs, and scalp, as these areas can be primary sites in patients of color. A comprehensive full-body skin exam remains the most critical tool for all patients.",
